menu "CSI band sweep configuration"

    choice CSI_SWEEP_BAND
        prompt "Bands to sweep"
        default CSI_SWEEP_BAND_BOTH

        config CSI_SWEEP_BAND_BOTH
            bool "Both (2.4 GHz then 5 GHz)"
        config CSI_SWEEP_BAND_24
            bool "2.4 GHz only"
        config CSI_SWEEP_BAND_5
            bool "5 GHz only"
    endchoice

    config CSI_SWEEP_DWELL_MS
        int "Milliseconds to dwell on each channel"
        range 100 10000
        default 800
        help
            The sweep is passive: it counts what other people transmit, so a
            short dwell on a quiet channel proves nothing. 800 ms across 32
            channels is roughly a 26 second pass.

            Raise it to 2000 or more if you are trying to establish that a
            channel really is empty rather than merely quiet at that moment.
            Beacons alone arrive about every 100 ms per AP, so anything above a
            few hundred milliseconds will find an AP if one is there.

endmenu
